  "response_text": "Always running the highest-priority thread can lead to starvation\u2014lower-priority threads might never get CPU time if a higher-priority thread is always ready. This breaks fairness and makes the system non-responsive to background tasks. In embedded systems, all threads may have important but different roles (e.g., logging, UI, communications), so starving some tasks can cause system failure. A better approach would be priority with aging or priority round-robin, which balances urgency with fairness.\\n",
